The '''Second Spire''' was an old temple,<ref name="Battle of Jedha script" /> and arrowhead of [[stone]]work that was associated with a particular [[Religion|faith]] that<ref name="GotW" /> by [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> was all but forgotten. It was one of the tallest structures in [[Jedha City|Holy City]], and was still a third of the height of [[Temple of the Kyber]].<ref name="GotW" /> By [[382 BBY]],<ref name="Battle of Jedha date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[The High Republic: The Battle of Jedha]]'' to [[382 BBY]].</ref> the spire had been abandoned, but was refitted for the intended [[Summit on Jedha|signing]] of a [[Eiram–E'ronoh peace treaty|treaty]] between delegates from the [[Eiram and E'ronoh War|warring]] [[planet]]s [[Eiram]] and [[E'ronoh]].<ref name="Battle of Jedha script" /> During this [[time]], [[Jedi Master]] [[Leebon]] was required to skip a meeting of the [[Convocation of the Force]] as she was needed at the spire.<ref name="Peace and Unity">{{StoryCite|story=Peace and Unity|book=The High Republic (2022) 1}}</ref> 

However, the Second Spire was later [[Attack on the peace summit|bombed]] during the peace summit by members of the [[Brotherhood of the Ninth Door]], a [[Dark side of the Force|dark side]] group working with the [[Path of the Open Hand]] [[Religion|cult]] and [[Graf family]] pariah [[Tilson Graf]]. The summit's mediator, [[Morton San Tekka]], was killed in the attack, and the summit was rescheduled with Graf as a new mediator. However, a riot was incited by Path [[Herald (title)|leader]] [[Werth Plouth]] in the [[Square of the Supplicants]] during the summit. At the same time that rioters reached the Spire, a member of the Brotherhood of the Ninth Door broke in and assassinated [[E'roni]] [[ambassador]] [[Tintak]]. This all caused the forces of Eiram and E'ronoh in the Spire to begin attacking each other, starting the [[Battle of Jedha]].<ref name="Battle of Jedha script" />

By 1 BBY,<ref name="Date" /> the Second Spire, along with the [[First Spire]], had been closed and sealed off by the [[Galactic Empire]], and far fewer [[pilgrim]]s made attempts to visit the spire compared with the Temple of the Kyber.<ref name="GotW" />

